/id #edb/ref 17592186547738} {:answer/id #uuid "d14fd27f-86c4-5e50-9a38-a0fb3d5e73f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d73b089-4ec1-5abd-9c8a-c1cd4ac044b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547453} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ea577f4-edb3-5442-83b4-270041c2560c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547880} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac76d92-c7a8-5564-a20c-1e1847021666" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }(2{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547338} {:answer/id #uuid "0b5395db-b568-583c-8baf-fc07a58b23ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(2{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547339} {:answer/id #uuid "216767d5-53a2-5586-91eb-86d1e28fc889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(2{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547383} {:answer/id #uuid "39cd9beb-045a-55b9-821e-f6e11f258364" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(2{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547438} {:answer/id #uuid "3d00e3a0-859a-5901-9e18-ad6053b930f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }(2{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547451} {:answer/id #uuid "64498cad-44bc-56c7-b4bd-80ae810d3b80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(2{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "216767d5-53a2-5586-91eb-86d1e28fc889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(2{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547383} :answer-field/id #uuid "b78b1748-be2b-5325-ae26-b27a57068806" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3db32c22-3de8-5264-9b28-9916a3aeb5f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-340659" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=2{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${b}_{3}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{3} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{b}_{3}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{sin}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi -0)-\\frac{1}{12}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={b}_{3}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩ \\\\ {b}_{3} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩} \\\\ {b}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(2{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526085 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166963 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fadf4f64-3569-56b2-98e1-f6681892054a" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Orthogonality of Sines and Cosines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b761040-6bc5-5857-9c79-db2a13d27611" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525349} {:answer/id #uuid "edaa6194-fdee-5a52-85e0-2ed9f495bf4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edaa6194-fdee-5a52-85e0-2ed9f495bf4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525797} :answer-field/id #uuid "55543445-1727-5019-a16d-94fb1228f51e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525890} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c5912f1-7503-5114-bd94-c09318d2aa64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525231} {:answer/id #uuid "bf39a84a-5b39-5bb5-8f67-5b65a043baf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525695} {:answer/id #uuid "ed84a8fc-5d46-52dc-beb9-dfab6973e8cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525796} {:answer/id #uuid "fea342fe-4c4d-5c10-87ec-9f65ac0a4202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fea342fe-4c4d-5c10-87ec-9f65ac0a4202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525840} :answer-field/id #uuid "f22a4739-c628-52a9-ae16-699a277e6c24" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525971}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d85f2141-c945-5a8d-a74b-f86923a41441" :question/math-academy-id "q-340668" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ defined above, select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),1⟩=$ \n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)$ and $g(x)=1$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the inner product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),1⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-5\\pi )) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(0-0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)$ and $g(x)=1$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413393 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166963 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fadf4f64-3569-56b2-98e1-f6681892054a" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Orthogonality of Sines and Cosines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83094832-5120-528d-afe1-e8471b128d10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413363} {:answer/id #uuid "8ecad901-e457-5a7f-9933-d49a111a2f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413365} {:answer/id #uuid "a32e9ce1-165d-5035-b70b-2b4a5c8fee66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413368} {:answer/id #uuid "c163715f-e3af-5949-bcaf-b925167883f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413372} {:answer/id #uuid "fdc708f1-6571-5820-8c85-8be92dcce522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83094832-5120-528d-afe1-e8471b128d10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413363} :answer-field/id #uuid "1674a71f-884a-5a58-b12e-e9101bb4e574" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413385} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69cbe4e6-0948-5e9f-9176-a7c91f104c4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413358} {:answer/id #uuid "cd85ba26-4b7d-5d1f-bcc0-b9b5eeb786e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69cbe4e6-0948-5e9f-9176-a7c91f104c4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413358} :answer-field/id #uuid "db85f0d1-90c6-55e8-8218-c8897868d5ec" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0c2afbe9-632c-56a2-8877-4a2cf3a61d97" :question/math-academy-id "q-340679" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-7\\pi ))+\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3\\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(-1-(-1))+\\frac{1}{6}(-1-(-1)) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314996 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166963 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fadf4f64-3569-56b2-98e1-f6681892054a" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Orthogonality of Sines and Cosines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0daa087f-f323-5faa-a4e9-604ca35655a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312072} {:answer/id #uuid "1ec12530-fa82-5a17-a031-79a932c12dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ec12530-fa82-5a17-a031-79a932c12dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312207} :answer-field/id #uuid "23144716-14d7-5695-8ba6-29c9023690ee" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314101} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01360f92-7aa0-57d4-94ae-48f679e6d3c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311969} {:answer/id #uuid "0a9294e7-86af-5ec9-91da-9b7b9c3babbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312055} {:answer/id #uuid "b896a225-dd54-54b0-a287-c64e84fd2786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313409} {:answer/id #uuid "e6b05747-a692-5a14-91bd-a0c5e65ea7f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313804} {:answer/id #uuid "f00630e3-28fe-5d6a-9eb6-0f4d51ed9ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f00630e3-28fe-5d6a-9eb6-0f4d51ed9ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313898} :answer-field/id #uuid "dad5592b-c4ca-59f6-a22d-0e05b8530ab1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314616}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "25666762-6caa-548c-81d4-5ffe0a56d215" :question/math-academy-id "q-340681" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-7\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(-1-(-1))-\\frac{1}{2}(-1-(-1)) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166962 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "544f5154-5213-5898-a45d-4546bc8004c8" :knowledge-point/title "Understanding the Periodic Extension of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fa4792b-5b15-527a-992e-0d96170ab1aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450530} {:answer/id #uuid "f9461d03-b412-574d-9841-bce08dceb69a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9461d03-b412-574d-9841-bce08dceb69a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450531} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a1e573c-09ca-594f-a9ba-3b2660311b38" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451219} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d83cac8f-f51f-527a-b720-44ad32045870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450532} {:answer/id #uuid "333f0aac-7943-517c-87c6-fb5685a1c0fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d83cac8f-f51f-527a-b720-44ad32045870" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450532} :answer-field/id #uuid "611505c9-97d8-564c-8e0d-e557fa6b701e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451220} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01e9805a-d060-5fce-8210-0537d29aaf51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450534} {:answer/id #uuid "7605eb1c-ab43-5593-8185-dd779575eaf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7605eb1c-ab43-5593-8185-dd779575eaf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450535} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1ba82cd-be54-5931-a8f3-844d7c5db9bc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451221}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ea143c38-1de5-5608-b272-c1150223e597" :question/math-academy-id "q-341232" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ for $x\\in R.$ Suppose $f(x)$ is the $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ from $x\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ to $x\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R$\n- **II.** $f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in R$\n- **III.** $f(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})=f(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ for all $x\\in R$" :question/worked-solution "Since $f$ is the $\\pi /2$-periodic extension of $F,$ we have  \n\n- $f(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})=f(x)$ for all $x\\in R,$ and\n\n- $f(x)=F(x)$ for all $x\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nWith that in mind, we examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. This is exactly the definition of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$-periodicity:\n\n$$\nf(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})=f(x)\n$$\n\nfor all $x\\in R.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, take $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$ Using the periodicity of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=f(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{2})=f(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=F(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhile\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{4})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(x)\\ne F(x)$ for $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $f$ is $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$-periodic, any shift by a multiple of its period returns the same value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})=f(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,f(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=f((x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{\\pi }{2})=f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince both sides equal $f(x),$ the statement is true for all $x\\in R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167291 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166964 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "304c015d-cbb6-5989-a102-d6f0f5f38604" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Expressions For Fourier Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ef2209e-3d8f-5297-ad7a-edc869e85aa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+9x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413355} {:answer/id #uuid "5ed25c1f-08d5-5b38-8bf8-b0a0bfd412ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+9x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413357} {:answer/id #uuid "88d440e0-29f7-5376-a757-92d36791c9cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{2}+9x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413364} {:answer/id #uuid "c052414d-62b2-5ddf-8d38-b8519a51bb8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{2}+9x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413371} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ac8e7f-277f-5ca0-83dd-f93b1ee8e219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+9x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ed25c1f-08d5-5b38-8bf8-b0a0bfd412ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+9x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413357} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a51accb-bbae-52f7-8c5d-2c3c83aae97b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413387} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "281d8718-96cc-5786-9125-bdda8d8dfa5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413354} {:answer/id #uuid "734b3ad1-94c6-5ccc-a8b8-d77fb92327cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413360} {:answer/id #uuid "74949511-a7ef-5835-b1ed-11c9565189c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413361} {:answer/id #uuid "b4aa1927-cea8-52e9-87f5-49a49eb90e82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413369} {:answer/id #uuid "f656d122-43f2-55e3-b008-141d9bf4c09e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4aa1927-cea8-52e9-87f5-49a49eb90e82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413369} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2554085-77fe-5157-9ee0-fb327d6f9788" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413390} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cdcf984-3000-5dc4-be61-ef3673edd14c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413356} {:answer/id #uuid "7d216d93-03a2-52c7-8109-b053ea99a0b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413362} {:answer/id #uuid "c04eff61-d1a2-5922-831e-05e57e1cedbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413370} {:answer/id #uuid "de6a0d2c-a56d-5bb1-9b1c-cd4e2312cdc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413376} {:answer/id #uuid "ffd7dac4-b5f5-51c0-9495-3c31b7bdebf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨1,1⟩}{⟨f(x),1⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5cdcf984-3000-5dc4-be61-ef3673edd14c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413356} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe88487e-f897-504c-b0b7-1ea54245c515" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5082df1a-d560-5493-a305-43900a17419a" :question/math-academy-id "q-341306" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}+9x$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{0}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),1⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),1⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),1⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨1,1⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[x]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),1⟩ & =\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩ \\\\ {a}_{0} & =\\frac{2⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩} \\\\ {a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{2}+9x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315084 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166963 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fadf4f64-3569-56b2-98e1-f6681892054a" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Orthogonality of Sines and Cosines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a485b2b2-9921-5fd5-bd9d-f8899940f0fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313268} {:answer/id #uuid "cd2136e8-d9d6-5af6-a549-5e509b077f3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a485b2b2-9921-5fd5-bd9d-f8899940f0fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313268} :answer-field/id #uuid "45a717f2-4ea4-5657-bb93-c452e09b74ae" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314202} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14b12c1a-93ae-5bc6-9fe8-42c8eda21ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312119} {:answer/id #uuid "1b4f5c80-0a03-57e7-8507-5198d48c6bfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312177} {:answer/id #uuid "4693d13b-e7f3-533f-a819-ee280e597461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312552} {:answer/id #uuid "7f7359a2-3aa5-59d3-a824-65f7cf6dc11f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14b12c1a-93ae-5bc6-9fe8-42c8eda21ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312119} :answer-field/id #uuid "98de6f2f-ef74-5be0-a949-95ef2c54203f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "22b987d7-9005-5317-ab10-48027150c40e" :question/math-academy-id "q-341340" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ defined above, select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We begin by using the product-to-sum identity\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{14}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(14\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))+\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{14}(1-1)+\\frac{1}{2}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ and $g(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product."}]}
